B.hoT=new A.ei("y10","10-year Treasury yield",u.ty,"Growth or inflation expectations are rising, the Fed is expected to stay tight, or investors want more pay for holding long bonds. Existing bond prices fall.","Growth fears, falling inflation expectations or a rush to safety. Existing bond prices rise.","Long-term borrowing costs rising \u2014 pressure on valuations.","Long yields falling \u2014 growth fear or easing inflation.","At {v}, the 10-year has moved at an ordinary pace over the last three months.","At {v}, the 10-year has swung half a point or more in three months \u2014 borrowing costs are repricing.","At {v}, the 10-year has swung a full point or more in three months \u2014 a bond-market shock.",B.doX,B.d9N,"Rate-sensitive sectors (real estate, utilities, small caps) and long-duration growth stocks feel it most; banks gain from a steeper curve.",B.d5Y,B.dwF)
