B.hpm=new A.ei("s2s10","10-year minus 2-year spread",u.bj,"The curve is steepening: long rates rising faster than short ones. After an inversion this usually comes as the Fed cuts, and it often arrives close to the start of a slowdown.","The curve is flattening, and below zero it is inverted: the market sees tighter policy now and weaker growth later.","Curve steepening \u2014 often follows an inversion as cuts arrive.","Curve flattening toward or deeper into inversion.","At {v}, the curve has a normal upward slope \u2014 the market is not signalling near-term trouble.","At {v}, the curve is nearly flat \u2014 it is close to the point where short rates exceed long ones.","At {v}, the curve is inverted (short rates above long rates), historically an early recession warning.",B.dfB,B.dmg,"Banks are the textbook loser from inversion; defensives such as utilities and staples tend to lead when it persists.",B.daa,B.d6Q)
B.i9L=new A.L("0 to +0.5 pp","Flat (watch).")
B.i86=new A.L("Below 0 pp","Inverted (stress). Academic and Fed research has found this spread, with a lead of roughly a year, to be a strong recession indicator in US data.")
