B.IP=new A.D("expand",B.a9,'Row only: this DIRECT child is wrapped in `Expanded` (flex 1), growing to fill the row\'s slack width instead of sizing to its own content \u2014 the only way to get a true flexible gap in a `row` ("title left, icons pinned right"), since Row has no working `mainAxis: "spaceBetween"` when its own incoming width is unbounded (a row inside a shrink-wrapping column gets an unbounded main axis, where spaceBetween has nothing to distribute into). A `spacer` node with `expand: true` is the usual case; any row child can opt in.',B.l,null,!1)
