B.i1c=new A.D("filter",B.W,"Opt-in row scope for `nodesTable` (and, unless `dataFilter` overrides it, `dataTable` too) \u2014 same shape as `bubl`'s filter: {column, value} or {column, in:[...]}; `value`/each `in` entry may be a token ($selected:<table>, $rowId, $playerId). Absent = all rows (unchanged behavior); resolved value/set EMPTY = no rows, never all. A node/data row freshly created while a resolved scalar {column, value} filter is scoping the view is stamped with that column:value so it stays in scope.",B.l,null,!1)
B.b40=new A.D("dataFilter",B.W,"Opt-in override of `filter` for `dataTable` only, when the data table scopes on a different column than `nodesTable`. Same shape as `filter`. Absent = `dataTable` falls back to `filter`.",B.l,null,!1)
B.b4w=new A.D("scopeColumn",B.L,"Opt-in ENGINE scope filter for `nodesTable` \u2014 the same convention the `explorer` node's `scopeColumn` reads via `activeScope`, so a canvas bound to a scoped table (e.g. a File > Board > nodes chain) shows only the open file/board's nodes even when no ancestor explorer for that hop happened to mount. Distinct from `filter` (a token-resolved value/set filter); the two may combine. Absent = unchanged behavior.",B.l,null,!1)
