B.hPX=new A.D("dragSelect",B.a9,"Dropdown only: render as a dense select that supports press-drag-release as one continuous gesture \u2014 press the trigger, drag down the option list, release on a choice \u2014 in addition to plain tap-open/tap-select. The open list FLOATS (an OverlayEntry anchored to the trigger, opening below or above by available room), wrapped in OverlayGestureShield so it stays a hit-opaque, web-DOM-dead-zoned surface \u2014 a drag over it can never fall through to a map underneath, and the trigger's own laid-out size never changes when the list opens. Keyboard: arrow-up/down move the highlight (opening the list if closed), enter/space opens or commits, escape closes.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hS8=new A.D("triggerWidth",B.aS,'Dropdown only: cap the closed trigger\'s label width (logical px), independent of the header/row it sits in \u2014 a short-word section selector ("Map", "Areas") does not need the 140px default. The full label is still readable in the OPEN list.',B.l,null,!1)
